translations.text:
I find no peace, nor am I allowed to wage war;

devoured by fire, I suffer cold;

I embrace a world and remain empty;

I hurl myself toward heaven, and earth holds me fast.


I am not free, yet no prison confines me;

I see without light and yearn to speak without a voice;

I fear without hope, I laugh without joy;

nothing gives me courage, nothing terrifies me.


I seek danger when I beg for help;

feeling myself die, I find myself strong;

I mean to be brave, yet weep in weakness.


Thus my strange fate is fulfilled:

always at the feet of the beauty I adore,

who wants neither my life nor my death.
